Suppose that $a$ acted as a <hyperbolic isometry of a tree>, with <translation length> $\tau>0$. Nonzero powers have the same axis and
$$
\ell(a^m)=m\tau,
\qquad
\ell(a^n)=n\tau.
$$
Translation length is invariant under conjugacy, whereas the defining relation in the <Baumslag-Solitar group> says that $a^m$ and $a^n$ are conjugate. Hence $m\tau=n\tau$, contradicting $m\ne n$. Therefore $a$ acts elliptically in every combinatorial tree action.

